---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Canlander
pageClass: home
---
{%- from "partials/macros.njk" import mtgcard, quote, decktile -%}
{%- set vault = [
  { name: "Black Lotus", pts: 7 },
  { name: "Ancestral Recall", pts: 8 },
  { name: "Time Walk", pts: 5 },
  { name: "Mox Sapphire", pts: 3 },
  { name: "Mana Drain", pts: 1 },
  { name: "Strip Mine", pts: 1 }
] -%}
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero__lamp" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="wrap hero__grid">
    <div class="hero__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Canadian Highlander · 100 cards · one of each · 1v1</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title">Play anything.<br><em>Just not everything.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero__lede">Black Lotus is legal here. So is Time Walk. So is nearly every card printed since 1993. There's just one catch: you get ten points, and the best cards in Magic aren't free.</p>
      <div class="hero__actions">
        <a class="btn btn--brass" href="/learn/">Learn the format</a>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/play/">Find a game this weekend <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="vault" data-vault data-budget="10">
      <div class="vault__head">
        <p class="vault__title">The vault is open.</p>
        <p class="vault__sub">Pick what you'd play. You have ten points.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vault__grid" role="group" aria-label="Pick cards from the vault, up to ten points">
        {%- for c in vault %}
        <button class="vault__item" type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-pts="{{ c.pts }}" data-name="{{ c.name }}" style="--i:{{ loop.index0 }}">
          <span class="vault__tag" aria-hidden="true"><span>{{ c.pts }}</span></span>
          {{ mtgcard(c.name, null, "normal", true) }}
          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ c.name }}, {{ c.pts }} points</span>
        </button>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="vault__wallet">
        <div class="vault__meter" aria-hidden="true">{% for i in range(0, 10) %}<i></i>{% endfor %}</div>
        <p class="vault__status" data-vault-status aria-live="polite"><b data-vault-left>10</b> points left</p>
      </div>
      <a class="vault__next link-arrow" href="/build/" data-vault-next hidden>Now find the other ninety-odd cards <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="ticker" data-countdown="{{ site.nextPointsUpdate }}">
      <a class="ticker__cell" href="{{ site.official.articles }}">
        <span class="ticker__k">Next points update</span>
        <span class="ticker__v"><time datetime="{{ site.nextPointsUpdate }}">{{ site.nextPointsUpdate | longDate }}</time> <span class="ticker__count" data-countdown-out></span> <span class="ext" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
      </a>
      {%- set latestPoints = collections.news | firstOfKind("Points update") %}
      <a class="ticker__cell ticker__cell--wide" href="{{ latestPoints.url }}">
        <span class="ticker__k">Latest points change</span>
        <span class="ticker__v">{{ latestPoints.data.title }}</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ticker__cell" href="{{ site.official.points }}">
        <span class="ticker__k">Official points list</span>
        <span class="ticker__v">{{ points.list.length }} cards cost points <span class="ext" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section hooks">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">§ 1 &nbsp;The pull</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Play it once and <em>everything else feels small.</em></h2>
      <p class="section__lede">Ask anyone who plays what keeps them coming back. You'll hear one of these.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="hook">
      <div class="hook__cards hook__cards--three" aria-hidden="true">
        {{ mtgcard("Time Walk", 5, "normal") }}{{ mtgcard("Mox Sapphire", 3, "normal") }}{{ mtgcard("Mana Drain", 1, "normal") }}
      </div>
      <div class="hook__text">
        <p class="hook__n mono">01</p>
        <h3 class="hook__t">The cards behind the glass.</h3>
        <p>You know the ones. The cards you've only ever seen in binders, price guides and old tournament photos. Here they're sleeved up, on the table, getting cast.</p>
        {{ quote(quotes.nonsense) }}
        <a class="link-arrow hook__more" href="/build/#points">See what they cost <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hook hook--flip">
      <div class="hook__cards hook__cards--three" aria-hidden="true">
        {{ mtgcard("Ancestral Recall", 8, "normal") }}{{ mtgcard("Demonic Tutor", 3, "normal") }}{{ mtgcard("Strip Mine", 1, "normal") }}
      </div>
      <div class="hook__text">
        <p class="hook__n mono">02</p>
        <h3 class="hook__t">Ten points. A thousand arguments.</h3>
        <p>Lotus, or three Moxen? Ancestral, or a tutor and a Drain? Every deck answers differently, and every answer starts a debate at the table.</p>
        {{ quote(quotes.tension) }}
        <a class="link-arrow hook__more" href="/build/">Spend your first ten <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hook">
      <div class="hook__cards hook__cards--three" aria-hidden="true">
        {{ mtgcard("Snapcaster Mage", 0, "normal") }}{{ mtgcard("Brainstorm", 0, "normal") }}{{ mtgcard("Lightning Bolt", 0, "normal") }}
      </div>
      <div class="hook__text">
        <p class="hook__n mono">03</p>
        <h3 class="hook__t">No game plays out twice.</h3>
        <p>A hundred cards, one of each. The game you play tonight will never happen again, and that's exactly the point.</p>
        {{ quote(quotes.hopkins) }}
        <a class="link-arrow hook__more" href="/learn/#playing">How a game unfolds <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hook hook--flip">
      <div class="hook__cards hook__cards--three" aria-hidden="true">
        {{ mtgcard("Swords to Plowshares", 0, "normal") }}{{ mtgcard("Thalia, Guardian of Thraben", 0, "normal") }}{{ mtgcard("Psychic Frog", 1, "normal") }}
      </div>
      <div class="hook__text">
        <p class="hook__n mono">04</p>
        <h3 class="hook__t">A deck you keep for years.</h3>
        <p>Nothing rotates. Alpha sits next to last week's preview. The deck you build this winter is the one you'll still be tuning in five years.</p>
        {{ quote(quotes.salahub) }}
        <a class="link-arrow hook__more" href="/story/">Where it all began <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hook">
      <div class="hook__cards hook__cards--three" aria-hidden="true">
        {{ mtgcard("Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer", 0, "normal") }}{{ mtgcard("Force of Will", 0, "normal") }}{{ mtgcard("Fable of the Mirror-Breaker", 0, "normal") }}
      </div>
      <div class="hook__text">
        <p class="hook__n mono">05</p>
        <h3 class="hook__t">Just you, and them.</h3>
        <p>One opponent. Twenty life. No commander, no politics, no waiting for a pod. And a tournament every weekend, if you want one.</p>
        {{ quote(quotes.novelty) }}
        <a class="link-arrow hook__more" href="/play/">Find this weekend's game <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hook hook--flip">
      <div class="hook__cards hook__cards--three" aria-hidden="true">
        {{ mtgcard("Black Lotus", 7, "normal") }}{{ mtgcard("Timetwister", 0, "normal") }}{{ mtgcard("Sol Ring", 3, "normal") }}
      </div>
      <div class="hook__text">
        <p class="hook__n mono">06</p>
        <h3 class="hook__t">The biggest binder doesn't win.</h3>
        <p>Everyone gets the same ten points, and a proxy costs exactly what a real Lotus does. (Timetwister, by the way, costs zero.)</p>
        {{ quote(quotes.brewer) }}
        <a class="link-arrow hook__more" href="/play/#proxies">Play tonight, for free <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="bigquote">
      <blockquote><p>“The most fun Constructed format I've ever played.”</p></blockquote>
      <figcaption><span class="q__who">{{ quotes.sutcliffe.who }}</span>, writing for <a href="{{ quotes.sutcliffe.url }}">Wizards of the Coast</a> in 2016</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section indexcard-section section--rule">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split__aside">
      <p class="eyebrow">§ 2 &nbsp;The rules</p>
      <h2 class="h2">The whole format fits on an index card.</h2>
      <p>If you know how to play Magic, you're five rules away from playing Canlander. Everything interesting lives in the points list.</p>
      <a class="link-arrow" href="/learn/#rules">The rules, in more detail <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="indexcard" role="group" aria-label="The rules of Canadian Highlander">
      <div class="indexcard__head">
        <span>Canadian Highlander</span>
        <span class="mono">Deck construction</span>
      </div>
      <ol class="indexcard__list">
        <li><b>100 cards</b>, minimum. No maximum, but you'll want exactly 100.</li>
        <li><b>One copy of each card</b>, except basic lands and cards that say otherwise.</li>
        <li><b>No sideboard.</b> One game, one deck, no companions.</li>
        <li><b>Ten points</b> to spend on cards from the points list. Everything else is free.</li>
        <li><b>Banned:</b> the Vintage banned list, plus a few oddballs (stickers, Acorn, silver border, dexterity, sub-games).</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="indexcard__foot">Two players. Twenty life. Vintage card pool.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--felt pricelist">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">§ 3 &nbsp;The price list</p>
        <h2 class="h2">The seven most expensive cards in the format.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__lede">{{ points.list.length }} cards cost points. These seven cost five or more, which means you can afford one of them and not much else. <a href="/build/#points">See all {{ points.list.length }}</a>, or check the <a href="{{ site.official.points }}">official list</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pricelist__row">
      {%- for c in points.list %}{% if c.points >= 5 %}
      <a class="pricelist__card" href="{{ c.name | scryfallLink }}" rel="noopener">{{ mtgcard(c.name, c.points, "normal") }}<span class="pricelist__name">{{ c.name }}</span></a>
      {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="pricelist__note mono">Values as of the {{ points.asOfLabel }}. The next update is <a href="{{ site.official.articles }}">{{ site.nextPointsUpdate | longDate }}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section decks-section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">§ 4 &nbsp;Decks to steal</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Borrow a deck <em>tonight.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__lede">What the community is brewing right now. <a href="/decks/">See every deck</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="carousel" data-carousel>
      <div class="carousel__track" data-track tabindex="0" aria-label="Deck carousel">
        {%- for d in decks.decks | rotation %}
        <div class="carousel__slide">{{ decktile(d, decks.authors) }}</div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="carousel__controls">
        <button class="carousel__btn" type="button" data-prev aria-label="Previous decks">←</button>
        <span class="carousel__count mono" data-count></span>
        <button class="carousel__btn" type="button" data-next aria-label="Next decks">→</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section teasers">
  <div class="wrap teasers__grid">
    <a class="teaser teaser--story" href="/story/">
      <span class="teaser__art" style="background-image:url('{{ "Tinker" | cardImg("art_crop") }}')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="teaser__body">
        <span class="eyebrow">The story</span>
        <span class="teaser__title">A comic shop in Victoria. A Tinker problem. <em>A very good idea.</em></span>
        <span class="link-arrow">Read how it began <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
      </span>
    </a>
    <a class="teaser teaser--council" href="/council/">
      <span class="teaser__art" style="background-image:url('{{ "Mana Drain" | cardImg("art_crop") }}')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="teaser__body">
        <span class="eyebrow">The council</span>
        <span class="teaser__title">Seven volunteers decide what every card costs. <em>Meet them.</em></span>
        <span class="link-arrow">The council <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--rule">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">§ 5 &nbsp;Your first week</p>
      <h2 class="h2">From curious to your first match.</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step__n">01</span>
        <h3 class="step__t">Read the rules</h3>
        <p>Ten minutes. Then skim the points list so you know what costs what.</p>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/learn/">Learn <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step__n">02</span>
        <h3 class="step__t">Pick a deck</h3>
        <p>Grab a list above or from a recent event. Choose the one whose game plan sounds fun, not the one that sounds strongest.</p>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/decks/">Decks <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step__n">03</span>
        <h3 class="step__t">Play this weekend</h3>
        <p>Two Discord tournaments every Saturday and Sunday. Free to enter, proxies welcome.</p>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/play/">Where to play <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step__n">04</span>
        <h3 class="step__t">Make it yours</h3>
        <p>After ten games, swap the cards you were never happy to draw. That's when it starts to feel like your deck.</p>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/build/">Build guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--rule">
  <div class="wrap two-up">
    <div>
      <div class="section__head section__head--row">
        <h2 class="h3">News</h2>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/news/">All news <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <ul class="ledger">
        {%- for post in collections.news | limit(4) %}
        <li class="ledger__row">
          <time class="ledger__date mono" datetime="{{ post.date | isoDate }}">{{ post.date | shortDate }}</time>
          <a class="ledger__title" href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="section__head section__head--row">
        <h2 class="h3">Most useful links</h2>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/resources/">All resources <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <ul class="ledger">
        {%- for r in resources.items | featured | limit(6) %}
        <li class="ledger__row">
          <span class="ledger__date mono">{{ r.url | domain }}</span>
          <a class="ledger__title" href="{{ r.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ r.name }} <span aria-hidden="true" class="ext">↗</span></a>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
